      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/08-carp-like-fishes-2-barbs-minnows-carps-goldfish-etc/barbus_cf_callipterus_en/",
      "html": "<p>The following information refers to the general keeping conditions of larger barb species. They prefer well-planted tanks (&gt; 80 cm) with open water for swimming.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/08-carp-like-fishes-2-barbs-minnows-carps-goldfish-etc/barbus_cf_callipterus_en/",
      "html": "<p>Barbs usually have no excessive requirements regarding food, but like other fish they enjoy an occasional addition of frozen or live food to a base diet of commercial flake food. One is then often surprised at the energy in a shoal of barbs if, for example, live water fleas are offered to them.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/08-carp-like-fishes-2-barbs-minnows-carps-goldfish-etc/barbus_cf_callipterus_en/",
      "html": "<p>They are social shoaling fish, which are best kept in groups of at least 7 individuals. Other peaceful, active fish are suitable tank mates.</p>"
    }
